            <ArticleTitle>Unexplained visual loss after lumbar spinal fusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>346-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases of visual loss after spinal fusion surgery are described. In both cases, surgery was lengthy, the patient's head was placed in a dependent position, and hemodilution and deliberate hypotension were combined. One patient was achondroplastic, the other obese. Possible risk factors associated with ischemic optic neuropathy after anesthesia and surgery are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
